---
import { Image } from "astro:assets";
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import "../styles/bolder.css";
import iphoneDuration from "../../../video/public/iphone-duration-45.png";
import iphoneSchedules from "../../../video/public/iphone-schedules.png";
import iphoneWebsites from "../../../video/public/iphone-websites.png";
import macDuration from "../../../video/public/mac-duration-45.png";
import macSchedules from "../../../video/public/mac-schedules.png";
import macWebsites from "../../../video/public/mac-websites.png";
---

<Base title="A little space. For what matters." pageClass="bolder" description="Posato blocks the websites and apps you choose for a timed pause on your Mac or iPhone, now or on a schedule. No Posato account, no analytics, and no Posato-operated server.">
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="hero-copy">
      <h1>A little space.<br /><span>For what matters.</span></h1>
      <div class="hero-details">
      <p class="lead">
        Posato blocks the websites and apps you choose for a timed pause on your Mac or iPhone,
        now or on a schedule, within the <a href="#limits">limits</a> below.
      </p>
      <p class="muted">No Posato account, no analytics, and no Posato-operated server.</p>
      <p class="download">
        <a href="https://github.com/dees91/posato/releases/latest"><img src="/badges/download-for-mac.svg" width="186" height="56" alt="Download Posato for Mac" /></a>
        <a href="https://apps.apple.com/app/posato/id6812237585"><img src="/badges/download-on-the-app-store.svg" width="186" height="56" alt="Download Posato on the App Store" /></a>
      </p>
      <p class="platforms">Posato for Mac and iPhone</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="hero-demo">
      <video
        class="hero-video"
        autoplay
        controls
        muted
        loop
        playsinline
        preload="metadata"
        width="1600"
        height="1000"
        poster="/media/hero-bolder-poster.jpg"
        aria-label="Posato demo: chosen websites, a 45-minute duration, a deliberate start, the Mac reporting restrictions active, optional iCloud sync between Mac and iPhone, and changes encrypted on the device before storage in private iCloud"
      >
        <source src="/media/hero-bolder.mp4" type="video/mp4" media="(min-width: 701px)" />
      </video>
      <img
        class="hero-poster"
        src="/media/hero-bolder-poster.jpg"
        width="1600"
        height="1000"
        alt="Posato on a Mac reporting restrictions active, with the session end time and an option to end early"
        fetchpriority="high"
      />
    </div>
</section>

  <section class="step" aria-labelledby="choose">
    <div class="step-copy">
    <h2 id="choose">Choose what to pause</h2>
    <p class="prose">
      Add exact website domains, then choose apps separately on each device. App choices stay on that
      device; only the shared app group's name syncs.
    </p>
    </div>
    <div class="shots">
      <div class="device device-mac shot-mac">
        <div class="device-screen">
          <Image
            src={macWebsites}
            widths={[480, 636, 960, 1272]}
            sizes="(max-width: 600px) 70vw, 36rem"
            alt="Mac Paused items screen showing the sample domains example.com and example.net"
          />
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="device device-iphone shot-iphone">
        <div class="device-screen">
          <Image
            src={iphoneWebsites}
            widths={[160, 330, 660]}
            sizes="(max-width: 600px) 24vw, 12rem"
            alt="iPhone Paused items screen with sample website choices"
          />
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="step" aria-labelledby="start">
    <div class="step-copy">
    <h2 id="start">Start a timed pause</h2>
    <p class="prose">
      Set a duration from <strong>5 minutes to 24 hours</strong>, review your choices, and start the
      session. Posato blocks your chosen websites and apps on that device, within the <a href="#limits">limits</a> below. The session ends at the selected time or when you deliberately end
      it early. On iPhone, restrictions can linger after the session ends. On a Mac, a one-time setup
      lets pauses and schedules start without asking for your password each time.
    </p>
    </div>
    <div class="shots">
      <div class="device device-mac shot-mac">
        <div class="device-screen">
          <Image
            src={macDuration}
            widths={[480, 636, 960, 1272]}
            sizes="(max-width: 600px) 70vw, 36rem"
            alt="Mac session setup with a 45-minute pause selected"
          />
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="device device-iphone shot-iphone">
        <div class="device-screen">
          <Image
            src={iphoneDuration}
            widths={[160, 330, 660]}
            sizes="(max-width: 600px) 24vw, 12rem"
            alt="iPhone session duration picker"
          />
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="step" aria-labelledby="schedules">
    <div class="step-copy">
    <h2 id="schedules">Plan pauses ahead</h2>
    <p class="prose">
      Add a schedule with a name, weekdays, and hours, such as weekday mornings from 9 to 11. It starts
      and ends on its own on each device you set up, even with Posato's window closed or the iPhone app
      closed. Skip the next one or end one early when plans change. Posato can tell you when a pause
      ends or when one starts on another device.
    </p>
    </div>
    <div class="shots">
      <div class="device device-mac shot-mac">
        <div class="device-screen">
          <Image
            src={macSchedules}
            widths={[480, 636, 960, 1272]}
            sizes="(max-width: 600px) 70vw, 36rem"
            alt="Mac Schedules screen with a weekday schedule named Deep work and a daily one named Evening reading"
          />
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="device device-iphone shot-iphone">
        <div class="device-screen">
          <Image
            src={iphoneSchedules}
            widths={[160, 330, 660]}
            sizes="(max-width: 600px) 24vw, 12rem"
            alt="iPhone Schedules screen with a weekday schedule named Deep work"
          />
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="muted">Screenshots are from the real apps and show sample choices.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="step" aria-labelledby="sync">
    <h2 id="sync">Share the session with iCloud</h2>
    <p class="prose">
      Choose <strong>Sync with iCloud</strong> on one Mac and one iPhone signed in to the same Apple
      Account to share your website list, sessions, and schedules. No QR code or invitation is needed.
      Sync is best effort, so a change may arrive late or not at all. A session started on your iPhone
      blocks on the Mac only after you resume it there. Update Posato on every device: once a schedule
      is saved, a device on an earlier version stops syncing.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="limits">
    <h2 id="limits">Limits</h2>
    <p class="prose">Posato adds deliberate friction; it is not a lock you cannot open.</p>
    <ul class="prose">
      <li>
        <strong>Mac:</strong> blocking works while Posato runs, including in the menu bar with its
        window closed. Quitting Posato stops it and new scheduled starts. Blocking needs administrator
        approval; after the one-time setup, starts no longer ask for it. Paused apps are quit, so save
        your work before a session starts. Website blocking
        covers Safari and Google Chrome Stable while they use the system proxy settings.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>iPhone:</strong> Restrictions can linger after a session ends. For sessions under 15
        minutes, they clear only when Posato is open at the end or the next time you open it.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Sync:</strong> Sync is best effort; a change may arrive late or not at all. If every copy of your workspace key is lost,
        synchronized data cannot be recovered.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p class="prose">
      Read the <a href="/limits/">full blocking and sync limits</a> for browser coverage, VPN and Private Relay behavior, resuming after sleep, and data recovery.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="privacy-section" aria-labelledby="privacy">
    <h2 id="privacy">Privacy</h2>
    <p class="prose">
      Posato's developer does not receive your data. Your websites, app choices, sessions, and schedules stay on
      your devices. If you turn on iCloud sync, changes are encrypted on your device before they are
      stored in your private iCloud database. On Mac, update checks go to GitHub Releases only after you agree.
      See the <a href="/privacy/">privacy policy</a>.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="note" aria-labelledby="availability">
    <h2 id="availability">Availability</h2>
    <p>
      Posato 1.2 for Mac is a signed and notarized download from <a href="https://github.com/dees91/posato/releases/latest">GitHub Releases</a>.
      It can check for new releases after you agree, and installing an update waits until your session has ended. To move from Posato 1.0,
      download the new version, quit Posato, and replace the application. The iPhone app is on the <a href="https://apps.apple.com/app/posato/id6812237585">App Store</a>. Posato targets macOS 15 or later on Apple silicon and iOS 18 or later.
    </p>
    <p class="download">
      <a href="https://github.com/dees91/posato/releases/latest"><img src="/badges/download-for-mac.svg" width="186" height="56" alt="Download Posato for Mac" /></a>
      <a href="https://apps.apple.com/app/posato/id6812237585"><img src="/badges/download-on-the-app-store.svg" width="186" height="56" alt="Download Posato on the App Store" /></a>
    </p>
  </section>
</Base>
